Specular patch to UnRAR 7.1.0 (vendor/unrar in unrar_sys 0.5.8): no user32.dll on Windows.
Applied after specular-password.patch.

What it changes
  os.hpp includes specular/specular_k32.hpp (copied next to the sources by build.rs) after
  the Windows headers. Its macros send CharLowerW, CharUpperW, OemToCharA, OemToCharBuffA,
  CharToOemA and CharToOemBuffW to kernel32 versions (LCMapStringW, MultiByteToWideChar,
  WideCharToMultiByte) in specular/specular_k32.cpp. isnt.cpp no longer asks WMI whether a
  Windows 11 build number is really Windows 10: IsWindows11OrGreater goes by the version
  alone, as UnRAR does when built by other compilers. It only decides whether a name like
  aux.txt is renamed when extracting to disk, which the decode host never does.

Why
  The sandboxed decode host disables Win32k system calls once started, and Windows refuses
  that (ERROR_WRITE_PROTECT) for a process that has loaded user32.dll, which these imports
  and COM's ole32/oleaut32 load at start-up. Without them the host runs with Win32k off;
  delay-loading them instead would end the process at UnRAR's first case comparison.

